  "reviewer_notes": "This is a survey/product-description paper about energy-management software (Energy Guide) rather than a single empirical case study. Concrete contexts appear only as illustrative examples: a pipe mill (intensity ratio, A1/M1), a two-factor dynamic-norm illustration (A1/M2, whose attachment to the pipe mill is inferred), a furnace at the Siempelkamp steelmaking plant in Germany (A2/M3), and a compressor station (A3/M4). No fitted coefficients, equations, fit statistics or dataset details are reported for any model; multi-factorial models are described generically as constructed automatically by the Energy Guide program, sometimes using neural-network or physical models. Model families for M2/M3/M4 recorded as 'other' because the paper says only 'multi-factorial statistical model' without specifying linearity.",
